                <pb facs="0399" n="291" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg291"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/601: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-04-17T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 17,
                                1927—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 17—4:04
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>443. Legation’s 273, March 28, 8 p.m. Americans who have left northern Honan
                    south of Yellow River report evacuation of the area by American citizens
                    complete except for two Catholic fathers who remain at Kaifeng.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
